   Hospitality (BIZMATOUR), Malacca, MALAYSIA, MAY 12-14, 2015},
Abstract = {Technical, Vocational, Education and Training (TVET) has been long
   viewed as a second class education and in fact, this field was having a
   cold acceptance anywhere in most any parts of the worlds. Fortunately,
   in this past few years, many has emphasis on TVET importance based on
   the supply-demand need of a country for skilled worker. Transition from
   least preferred to highly essential was proven to head by leaders with
   leadership. Certainly, leadership plays a significant role in this
   transformation. However, less information crafted on what actually these
   leaders done based on their true insight. This paper explored single
   view perception of higher ranking leader on how to manage perception in
   TVET, leadership roles, definition and compendium of practiced from the
   TVET orientation. Such exploration presented in description manner with
   in-vivo statements from participant with literature support.},
