Note = {International Conference of Environment, Landscape, European Identity /
   Annual Scientific Meeting of the Faculty-of-Geography, Bucharest,
   ROMANIA, NOV 04-06, 2011},
Organization = {Univ Bucharest, Fac Geog, Dept Reg Geog \& Environm; Natl Author Sci
   Res; Natl Univ Res Council; Intergraph Comp Serv},
Abstract = {Incompatible land-use and land-cover indicate the trend in territorial
   planning and generate instability conflicts leading to degradation in
   terms of environmental quality. Urban landscape structure Bucharest
   suburban area has changed lately, especially due to expansion of
   residential areas, the risks of a chaotic urban development. The
   consequences of this residential expansion have led malfunctions,
   outlining a disadvantage area due to environmental problems. In this
   context, areas are frequently located in the proximity of gas stations
   in Bucharest suburban area. This presents the relation between
   residential areas and gas stations in order to evaluate causes that led
   to proximity. Results have pointed out using a number of 60 gas stations
   (21 gas stations in residential and 39 in non-residential areas) the
   causes and the temporal dynamics of locational conflicts, that unplanned
   development and residential agglomeration are the main consequences of
   conflicts. In this respect of incompatible land-use and land-cover
   expansion, it is required an and hierarchy in order to start new
   coherent plans of space development. (c) 2011 Published by Elsevier B.V.
