Title = {Study and Analysis of the Structure Situations of the Workers Employed
   in Hamadan Cities Solid Waste Management},
Booktitle = {PROGRESS IN ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY, VOL II, PTS A AND B},
Year = {2009},
Pages = {2028-2031},
Note = {International Symposium on Environmental Science and Technology,
   Shanghai, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUN 02-05, 2009},
Organization = {Chinese Soc Environm Sci; Beijing Inst Technol; Donghua Univ; Key Lab
   Explos Sci \& Technol},
Abstract = {Changes in living pattern, population growth, industrialization and also
   increasing the process of urbanization in human societies has created
   new environmental problems such as air pollution, major issue related to
   solid waste and municipal wastewaters more than ever. Today management
   of municipal solid wastes is an inseparable part of management of
   metropolises and it is really unavoidable to plan for solving the
   relevant problems. Solid waste management and the engineering is one of
   the applied sciences. Using modem technologies in urban engineering and
   solid waste management is one of the ordinary methods of designing
   installations, adopting strategies and policy making in the field of
   health and environment. Although solid wastes have devastative
   influences on the society, citizens and the environment, it could be
   very useful as a valuable opportunity for production of goods, providing
   employment and rendering services. This research has been conducted to
   study the structure situations of employees working in solid waste
   management section in Hamadan city. To conduct this study, a
   questionnaire was. used for the purpose of collecting information. There
   were totally 40 questions in the questionnaire. Population of this
   research includes all employees (700) working in solid wastes management
   section of Hamadan city. Simple random sampling method has been used to
   conduct this research, and totally 270 completed questionnaires were
   gathered (n=270). The questionnaires' validity and reliability have been
   assessed and confirmed. Based on the obtained results, the mean
   age(Standard deviation) of interviewees was 36.74 (9.48) years. Also,
   Based on the results of analysis of Chi Square, the age of employees
   working in solid waste management section in the Hamadan city has
   significant effects on literacy level (p=0.001) and occupational
   diseases (p=0.003), whereas the age has not any significant effects on
   the level of career knowledge (p=0.453). Regarding the fact that the
   quality, activity and performance of employees working of municipal
   solid waste management has a very important role in the health of people
   and environmental protection, it is necessary to investigate the guild
   issues and training and promotion of occupational information in this
   social stratum.},
