Note = {22nd Congress of the International Ergonomics Association-IEA, SOUTH
   KOREA, AUG 25-29, 2024},
Abstract = {It is believed that people need to implement more pro-environmental
   behaviors (PEB) to protect the global environment. However, it is also
   known that even if people are aware of the necessity and importance of
   addressing environmental issues, it is difficult for them to implement
   PEB. Therefore, it is important to promote people's PEB through
   interventions. In this study, for promoting PEB, we proposed an
   intervention to increase self-perceptions of sympathy and altruism by
   using fake feedback and conducted an evaluation experiment. Intervention
   designed in this study includes two types of personality-check style
   questionnaire: one using personality ratings from a close friend, and
   the other using a behavior choice quiz designed to make people naturally
   choose kinder behavior. The results indicated the intervention method
   needs further improvement, especially for empathy, because the
   participants were not sufficiently convinced of the evaluation, but the
   method of using false feedback itself is considered feasible.},
