   IL, MAY 27-30, 2004},
Organization = {Amer Psychol Soc},
Abstract = {As students participate in diversity courses in greater numbers, it is
   important to understand the effects of these courses. Although other
   researchers have examined this topic, particularly with respect to
   stereotype reduction anal racial attitudes, we were interested in how a
   diversity course might also affect students' awareness of racism and
   White privilege. With both quantitative and qualitative measures, our
   results showed increases in awareness and in feelings of racial guilt
   and responsibility. These findings expand the existing literature and
   highlight important questions for future research.},
