Abstract = {Harvester technologies represent the second most common logging system
   in the Czech Republic. The high productivity of this technology is very
   necessary to cover its acquisition and operational cost. The aid of this
   study is the monitoring of the operation time and shift time of the
   middle power harvester UTC FI067. The chronometry was analyzed during
   the felling works in premature forest stands. These results are worked
   up for tree volume of coniferous species from 0.13 to 0.52 m(3)/tree,
   which require for manufacturing total time from 83 to 170 seconds. Total
   standards lies for intermediate (improvement, advanced) fellings within
   the interval 0.12 - 0.21 working hours/m(3).},
