Note = {9th International Conference on Emotions and Worklife (Emonet),
   Philadelphia, PA, JUL 30-31, 2014},
Abstract = {Shame is a common, yet seldom acknowledged emotion. Shame signals a
   threatened social bond in which the claim of as what one wants to be
   seen (i.e., the claim for a certain relational identity and relative
   status positioning) is neglected by the other party. Using a case study
   approach, this chapter provides insights into how shame shapes the
   relationship and leadership structure in organizations. The case used is
   based on a documentary TV show; hence this chapter also provides insight
   in the use of visual/TV material to gain insight in relational
   leadership dynamics.},
