   Junta Andalucia; Dutch Fdn Neural Networks},
Abstract = {The brain has to process and react to an enormous amount of information
   from the senses in real time. How is all this information represented
   and processed within the nervous system? A proposal of nonlinear and
   complex systems research is that dynamical attractors may form the basis
   of neural information processing. Here we show that this idea can be
   successfully applied to the human auditory system, and can explain our
   perception of pitch.},
