   the 21st Century, Coimbra, PORTUGAL, 2007},
Organization = {Wessex Inst Technol},
Abstract = {Within the framework of the SICURO research project, the main objective
   of this paper is to define the procedures to be planned and activated in
   emergencies in order to allow the evacuation of weak users (disabled,
   old persons, etc.) from the area affected by a disaster and design the
   optimal path for emergency vehicles to reduce evacuation times.
   Specification, calibration and validation of a path choice generation
   model in order to simulate the behaviour of emergency vehicle drivers at
   an urban level during an evacuation is proposed. We specify the factors
   that affect path choice behaviour and the two main approaches: one to
   one and many to one. The first regards the minimization of generalized
   cost of a path that connects an origin to a destination; the second
   instead considers the connection of one origin to many destinations. We
   also report some experimental results, obtained in the context of the
   SICURO Project, by applying the proposed model to a real road transport
   network at urban scale during a simulation of an evacuation.},
