@inproceedings{ WOS:000165528200020,
Author = {Abdullahi, MA},
Editor = {Aminipouri, B and Ghoddousi, J},
Title = {Harmony between scientific and religious perceptions on rain},
Booktitle = {PROCEEDINGS OF THE 8TH INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON RAINWATER CATCHMENT
   SYSTEMS, VOL 3: RAINWATER CATCHMENT FOR SURVIVAL: RELIGIOUS AND CULTURAL
   ASPECTS},
Year = {1997},
Pages = {203-208},
Note = {8th International Conference on Rainwater Catchment Systems, TEHRAN,
   IRAN, APR 25-29, 1997},
Organization = {Minist Jihad E Sazandegi; Int Rainwater Catchment Syst Assoc},
Abstract = {His Almighty Allah reveals in the Holy Qur'an:
   `Do ye bring it down (in the from of precipitation) from the cloud or do
   We?
   The sacred religion of Islam and the holy Qur'an regard precipitation as
   Divine Gift. All the supplications also refer to rain as Divine
   Blessings. And so is the norm among believers. They relate every
   incident to the Volition of His Almighty Allah.
   There exists no difference between the religious beliefs and scientific
   concepts. by giving the matter a little thought, everything will become
   clear, that there is harmony between religious beliefs and scientific
   concepts.
   I. The concept of `Cause and Effect' are the indisputable principles in
   Philosophy.
   2. The Holy Qur'an clearly states, fully confirms and rightly supports
   the premise of `Cause and Effect'.
   3. Those who believe in Almighty God reason out that as every effect has
   cause behind it and that a chain of effects (events) and material causes
   cannot persist but originate from the First Cause, His Almighty Allah.
   4. The universe which is governed by the premise of `Cause and Effect',
   which is in fact the creation of His Almighty God, the omnipotent
   through His Own Volition. And as such no creature is independent of Mis
   Will. They are devoid of an independent course of action. All their acts
   originate from the First Cause from moment to moment, the Source of
   Power. So, we can conclude that no entity is off-limits from the Will of
   Almighty Lord. The creatures are incapable of performing any acts
   without His Volition.
   The water cycle begins with evaporation from the land surface, then it
   condenses in the form of clouds, and when the clouds become sufficiently
   pregnant, water falls in the form of precipitation. The cycle take place
   because it is Almighty Allah who Will it, so it be. It is therefore
   clear that there is no contradiction between science and religion. The
   Monotheist Philosophy is in line with the natural phenomenon taking
   shape following a set pattern. Both religious beliefs and scientific
   concepts concur in this respect.},
